    h1: "Should I build indoor or greenhouse cannabis cultivation?",
    answer: "This is the fundamental strategic decision in cultivation, and it is an engineering economics question. Indoor facilities control every variable - light, temperature, humidity, CO2 - and produce the most consistent premium flower, but they pay for every photon and every BTU with electricity. Greenhouses harvest sunlight, cutting lighting energy dramatically, but inherit the outdoor climate: they need blackout systems for photoperiod, aggressive humidity management, and supplemental lighting and heating to hold winter production. Hybrids - indoor for flower, greenhouse for veg, or sealed greenhouses with full environmental control - split the difference.",
