    h1: "How is HVAC designed for vertical rack cultivation?",
    answer: "Vertical farming multiplies revenue per square foot and multiplies the engineering challenge by the same factor. Two tiers of flowering canopy means twice the lighting watts, twice the transpiration, and half the air volume per plant to absorb it - stacked in a geometry where warm air rises past the upper tiers and humidity pools in the middle. Standard room-level HVAC design fails here: the room average can read perfectly while tier two sits five degrees warmer and fifteen percent more humid. The design must treat each tier as its own microclimate.",
